  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Reconnaissance — SP/IdP Metadata Discovery", "technique": "T1595", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-01 07:41:10 CEST, data.srcip=203.0.113.66 issued a burst of GET requests against the SSO Service Provider 10.108.57.184 probing well-known SAML metadata paths — /saml/metadata, /Shibboleth.sso/Metadata, /samlsso/metadata, /sp/sso/saml2/metadata, /.well-known/saml-configuration, /auth/saml/metadata — followed by IdP metadata probes (/idp/saml2/metadata, /simplesaml/saml2/idp/metadata.php). Wazuh web rules fired on the sequential 404/200 pattern from a single external source. The attacker is enumerating the federation topology: ACS endpoint URL, SP entityID and valid RelayState targets — the prerequisites for crafting a replayable SAML POST.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh web rule group (rule.groups containing 'web' / 'attack') fired with data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against data.dstip=10.108.57.184 hitting >6 distinct SAML-metadata URI paths within 3 minutes. Sequential metadata-path walking from a single external IP is the canonical federation-recon signature that precedes a SAML assertion replay.", "first_seen": "2026-05-01T07:41:10+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Credential Access — Forge Web Credentials: SAML Tokens", "technique": "T1606.002", "what_happened": "At 07:44:30 CEST, the same data.srcip=203.0.113.66 began POSTing base64-encoded SAMLResponse payloads to multiple Assertion Consumer Service endpoints — /saml/acs, /Shibboleth.sso/SAML2/POST, /samlsso, /sp/sso/saml2, /auth/saml/callback, /sso/saml2/acs. The assertions carry NameID alice.jones@corp.local and an Issuer of https://idp.corp.local/saml2/idp, but the IssueInstant is ~6 hours stale (2026-05-01T02:00:00Z) and there is no matching IdP-side sign-in event for that subject — the hallmark of a stolen/forged assertion replayed outside its validity window (Golden SAML / AiTM-captured token pattern). The attacker then retried with a freshly-stamped IssueInstant to probe the SP's assertion-age tolerance. Wazuh custom SAML rules fired on the aged IssueInstant, the missing/mismatched InResponseTo, and the repeated ACS POST volume from one IP.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rules 91300 (SAML assertion replay — IssueInstant older than tolerance), 91301 (SAML InResponseTo mismatch or missing) and 91302 (multiple SAML ACS POST attempts from single IP) fired in sequence with data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against data.dstip=10.108.57.184, plus Wazuh web rule 5716 (suspicious POST to /saml/acs). MITRE T1606.002 was attached by the rule. A SAML assertion for alice.jones@corp.local presented to the SP without any corresponding IdP authentication event for that subject is, by definition, a forged or replayed token.", "first_seen": "2026-05-01T07:44:30+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access / Lateral Movement — Post-SSO Application Access", "technique": "T1550", "what_happened": "From ~07:54 CEST, data.srcip=203.0.113.66 began issuing authenticated-looking GET requests carrying a session cookie to a wide spread of internal applications behind the SSO — /dashboard, /portal, /admin, /admin/users, /admin/settings, /api/internal/users, /api/internal/audit-log, /portal/documents, /portal/hr/payroll, /intranet, /intranet/it/assets, /confluence, /jira. This is the use-the-token step: if the replayed SAML assertion produced a valid SP session, the attacker rides it straight into sensitive internal apps (HR payroll, admin user management, internal audit log) without ever touching the IdP or knowing alice.jones' password. Wazuh web rules fired on the breadth of post-auth resource access from the same external IP within minutes.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh web rule group (rule.groups containing 'web') fired with data.srcip=203.0.113.66 against data.dstip=10.108.57.184 across >10 distinct internal application paths including /admin/* and /portal/hr/payroll within a 6-minute window, immediately following the Step-2 ACS POST burst. A single external IP fanning out across admin and HR resources seconds after a SAML ACS POST is the application-access signature of a successful Application Access Token abuse (T1550).", "first_seen": "2026-05-01T07:54:02+0200"}
  ],
